# NOT CONSULTED ANY MORE. Read the repository root's .dockerignore instead.
#
# A build reads the .dockerignore beside the CONTEXT ROOT, and this module's
# build context moved to the repository root: the module replaces
# libs/go/egresslib with ../../libs/go/egresslib, which a module-only context
# cannot reach. Every rule below is now carried by /.dockerignore, under
# "elitea-llm-gateway". Add a new rule THERE.
#
# The file stays so that a `podman build ... services/elitea-llm-gateway` run
# by hand behaves as it always did. That build cannot succeed today — it fails
# on the missing replacement — but a deleted ignore file is a rule that lapses
# without a trace, which is the failure this whole change is about.
#
# compiled binary (built inside the image, never copied from host)
elitea-llm-gateway

# version control
.git
.gitignore

# documentation
*.md

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store

# local artifacts and IDE files
*.local
.env
.env.*
*.log
tmp/
vendor/

# coverage output produced by `go test -coverprofile`
coverage.out

# go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, and internal/ are NOT excluded (kept for the build)
